        "<h2>Before you ask</h2><ul><li>A URL alias in lower case that follows the naming standard <strong>[org]-[location]-[department]-[site]</strong>, with a known location code. Otherwise the request is Returned - Naming standard.</li><li>Two different, enabled, internal people as primary and secondary owner. Otherwise it is Returned - Ownership invalid.</li><li>An Owners group and a Members group (Entra object IDs). Visitors and Guests groups are optional.</li><li>A sensitivity: General, Confidential or Highly Confidential.</li><li>Whether you need external sharing. It is off unless approved.</li></ul><p>Then {{new:Site Requests|add an item to Site Requests}}.</p>",
        "<h2>Who approves</h2><ul><li>The SharePoint service owner approves every new site.</li><li>InfoSec also approves when you ask for external sharing or the site is Highly Confidential.</li></ul>",
        "<h2>What you get</h2><p>Once the site is created, IT Operations applies and registers its Sites.Selected grant, then the baseline is applied: permissions through groups only, your secondary owner as a site admin, external sharing off unless approved, no custom script and your sensitivity label. Without the grant the request shows Provisioning failed and the service owner is told. The site is added to the {{list:Site Register}} with its first access review due in 90 days, and both owners are told.</p>"
